<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1922</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian Civil War was fought from 1917 to 1922 between the Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and a range of opponents, chiefly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">White movement</a>, with nationalist forces and foreign interventions also involved. The Bolsheviks defeated the White armies of Kolchak, Denikin, Yudenich and Wrangel and in 1922 founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>; millions died in the fighting, terror, famine and epidemics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war.jpg" alt="Russian Civil War" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Yanachka · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CWRArticleImage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
